<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pilaji Rao Gaekwad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1732</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pilaji Rao Gaekwad was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> commander who founded the power of the Gaekwad family in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. Serving under the Dabhade senapatis, he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songadh">Songadh</a> in 1721 and raided Mughal Gujarat from there until he was assassinated in 1732. His son Damaji Rao took Baroda, which became the capital of the Gaekwad state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pilaji-rao-gaekwad.jpg" alt="Pilaji Rao Gaekwad" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pilajirao_Gaikwad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
